ouble\ntarget/so-rel/release   -> next_double\ntarget/so-ubc/ubcheck   -> next_double\ntarget/release          -> next_double\nC                       -> next_double\n```\n\n`translation/rust_syms.txt` is regenerated by\n`tests/symbol_parity.rs::record_symbol_tables` on every run.\n\n## Verified result\n\n```\n$ bash run_all_configs.sh\ndeclared features: (none) -> combinations are {default, --no-default-features}\n-- PASS: cargo check [<default>]\n-- PASS: cargo test  [<default>] profiles=all\n-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=dev\n-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=release\n-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=ubcheck\n-- PASS: cargo check [--no-default-features]\n-- PASS: cargo test  [--no-default-features] profiles=all\n-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=dev\n-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=release\n-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=ubcheck\nALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED\n```\n\n47 tests per configuration (33 valid-path + 10 error-path + 4 symbol-parity),\n0 failures, 8 full `cargo test` runs.","originalFile":"# SYMBOLS.md — Phase A: exported-symbol surface\n\nGenerated mechanically from `nm -D` on both shared objects.\n\nBuild commands used:\n\n```sh\n# C\ncd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build \\\n  && cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .\n#  -> c_src/build/libharvest-work-c0iFqi.so\n#     (CMake derives the project/library name from the parent directory name)\n\n# Rust\ncd translation && cargo build --release\n#  -> translation/target/release/libnext_double_lib.so\n```\n\n## C translation units\n\nThe whole C library is a single translation unit:\n\n| C source file | translated to | status |\n|---------------|---------------|--------|\n| `c_src/src/lib.c`     | `translation/src/lib.rs` | fully translated |\n| `c_src/include/lib.h` | `translation/src/lib.rs` (`cn_rnd_t`) | fully translated |\n\nThere is **no** un-translated C module, so no Phase-A \"translate the missing\nsource\" work was required.\n\n## Defined (exported) dynamic symbols\n\n`nm -D --defined-only`:\n\n| # | symbol | C `.so` | Rust `.so` | kind | notes |\n|---|--------|---------|------------|------|-------|\n| 1 | `next_double`                 | `T` | `T` | text (function) | the only real API symbol; `double next_double(cn_rnd_t *)` |\n| 2 | `_ITM_deregisterTMCloneTable` | `w` | `w` | weak undefined | linker/ITM boilerplate, emitted by both toolchains |\n| 3 | `_ITM_registerTMCloneTable`   | `w` | `w` | weak undefined | linker/ITM boilerplate |\n| 4 | `__cxa_finalize@GLIBC_2.2.5`  | `w` | `w` | weak undefined | glibc boilerplate |\n| 5 | `__gmon_start__`              | `w` | `w` | weak undefined | profiling boilerplate |\n\n`nm -D --defined-only` output, verbatim:\n\n```\n# C\n0000000000001164 T next_double\n\n# Rust\n0000000000011c20 T next_double\n```\n\n## Symbol diff\n\n```\nC-defined-but-missing-in-Rust : (empty)\n```\n\n**0 missing symbols.** The diff has reached empty.\nEnforced automatically by the test `symbol_parity::c_defined_symbols_are_all_exported_by_rust`.\n\n## Symbols NOT part of the C `.so` that the Rust `.so` references\n\nThe Rust `cdylib` links the Rust standard library, so it has extra\n**undefined** (`U` / `w`) imports that the C `.so` does not:\n\n`_Unwind_*` (11 symbols), `__cxa_thread_atexit_impl`, `__errno_location`,\n`__tls_get_addr`, `abort`, `bcmp`, `calloc`, `close`, `dl_iterate_phdr`,\n`free`, `fstat64`, `getcwd`, `getenv`, `gettid`, `lseek64`, `malloc`,\n`memcpy`, `memmove`, `memset`, `mmap64`, `munmap`, `open64`,\n`posix_memalign`, `pthread_key_create`, `pthread_key_delete`,\n`pthread_setspecific`, `read`, `readlink`, `realloc`, `realpath`, `stat64`,\n`statx`, `strlen`, `syscall`, `write`, `writev`.\n\nAll of these are libc / libgcc-unwind symbols satisfied by the platform.\nNone is a *defined* symbol of the C `.so`, so none affects parity.\n\n**0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols in Rust.**\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` table**, therefore the\ncomplete set of feature combinations is:\n\n| # | combination | cargo invocation |\n|---|-------------|------------------|\n| 1 | default (empty) | `cargo test` |\n| 2 | `--no-default-features` (identical to #1, no features exist) | `cargo test --no-default-features` |\n\nBoth are exercised by `run_all_configs.sh`.\n\nIn addition, because the *compiled profile* changes real behaviour for a Rust\ntranslation (`overflow-checks`, `debug-assertions`, `panic=abort`), both\nprofiles of the cdylib are loaded and differentially tested:\n\n| profile | `overflow-checks` | `debug-assertions` | `panic` |\n|---------|-------------------|--------------------|---------|\n| `dev` (`target/so-dev/debug/libnext_double_lib.so`)     | on  | on  | unwind |\n| `release` (`target/so-rel/release/libnext_double_lib.so`) | off | off | abort |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":90,"oldLines":10,"newStart":90,"newLines":46,"lines":[" Both are exercised by `run_all_configs.sh`."," "," In addition, because the *compiled profile* changes real behaviour for a Rust","-translation (`overflow-checks`, `debug-assertions`, `panic=abort`), both","-profiles of the cdylib are loaded and differentially tested:","+translation (`overflow-checks`, `debug-assertions`, `panic=abort`), **three**","+cdylib profiles are built, loaded and differentially tested — every test runs","+against all three:"," ","-| profile | `overflow-checks` | `debug-assertions` | `panic` |","-|---------|-------------------|--------------------|---------|","-| `dev` (`target/so-dev/debug/libnext_double_lib.so`)     | on  | on  | unwind |","-| `release` (`target/so-rel/release/libnext_double_lib.so`) | off | off | abort |","+| profile | path | `opt-level` | `overflow-checks` | `debug-assertions` (Rust UB checks) | `panic` |","+|---------|------|-------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------|---------|","+| `dev`     | `target/so-dev/debug/libnext_double_lib.so`     | 0 | **on**  | off    | unwind |","+| `release` | `target/so-rel/release/libnext_double_lib.so`   | 3 | off     | off    | abort  |","+| `ubcheck` | `target/so-ubc/ubcheck/libnext_double_lib.so`   | 0 | **on**  | **on** | unwind |","+","+Every one of the three exports exactly `next_double`, matching the C:","+","+```","+target/so-dev/debug     -> next_double","+target/so-rel/release   -> next_double","+target/so-ubc/ubcheck   -> next_double","+target/release          -> next_double","+C                       -> next_double","+```","+","+`translation/rust_syms.txt` is regenerated by","+`tests/symbol_parity.rs::record_symbol_tables` on every run.","+","+## Verified result","+","+```","+$ bash run_all_configs.sh","+declared features: (none) -> combinations are {default, --no-default-features}","+-- PASS: cargo check [<default>]","+-- PASS: cargo test  [<default>] profiles=all","+-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=dev","+-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=release","+-- PASS: cargo test [<default>] profile=ubcheck","+-- PASS: cargo check [--no-default-features]","+-- PASS: cargo test  [--no-default-features] profiles=all","+-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=dev","+-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=release","+-- PASS: cargo test [--no-default-features] profile=ubcheck","+ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED","+```","+","+47 tests per configuration (33 valid-path + 10 error-path + 4 symbol-parity),","+0 failures, 8 full `cargo test` runs."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
